WEBVTT

00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:03.043
Sixty-six million years
ago, the dinosaurs had

00:00:03.053 --> 00:00:04.338
the worst day ever.

00:00:04.348 --> 00:00:07.505
An asteroid ten to fifteen kilometres wide

00:00:07.515 --> 00:00:09.643
slammed into the sea off the coast

00:00:09.653 --> 00:00:11.144
of what is now Mexico.

00:00:11.154 --> 00:00:13.430
It left a crater more than 150

00:00:13.440 --> 00:00:16.980
kilometres across, buried
today under the Yucatán

00:00:16.990 --> 00:00:17.899
Peninsula.

00:00:17.909 --> 00:00:19.911
The blast threw rock into the sky,

00:00:19.921 --> 00:00:22.168
and giant waves swept the coasts.

00:00:22.178 --> 00:00:23.831
Soot spread around the world and dimmed

00:00:23.841 --> 00:00:26.494
the Sun, so plants struggled to grow.

00:00:26.504 --> 00:00:28.679
About three quarters of all plant and

00:00:28.689 --> 00:00:32.166
animal species died out,
including every dinosaur

00:00:32.176 --> 00:00:33.467
except the birds.

00:00:33.477 --> 00:00:34.452
How do we know?

00:00:34.465 --> 00:00:36.380
A thin layer of clay, rich in

00:00:36.390 --> 00:00:39.005
the rare metal iridium, sits in rocks

00:00:39.015 --> 00:00:40.251
all over the world.

00:00:40.261 --> 00:00:42.526
Iridium is rare on Earth, but far

00:00:42.536 --> 00:00:44.466
more common in asteroids.

00:00:44.476 --> 00:00:46.591
So next time a pigeon walks past,

00:00:46.601 --> 00:00:47.626
remember:

00:00:47.676 --> 00:00:49.941
most scientists count it as a dinosaur

00:00:49.951 --> 00:00:50.976
that made it.
